WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.546 --> 00:00:01.379
(spacecraft zooming)

00:00:01.379 --> 00:00:03.750
- The US has been flying this spacecraft

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.330
since 2010, called the x-37B.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.570
It was recently loaded into a
Space X falcon heavy rocket,

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.660
and then blasted into space
on a super secret mission

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.430
right before the new year,

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.370
with very few details revealed
about where it's going,

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.250
how long it will be up there,
and what it'll be doing.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.350
And that happened just two weeks

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.470
after China launched its
own mysterious space plane.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.210
The classified nature of these missions

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.070
has fueled all kinds of speculation

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.960
about where these planes might be going

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.870
and whether they could
be used as space weapons.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.670
So I called a few experts to learn more

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.950
about what they might actually be up to.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.120
Here's what we know.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.970
Although the US's x-37B looks a lot

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.680
like NASA's former space shuttle,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.960
it's only about a quarter of the size.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.440
It's autonomous, and it doesn't
require a crew of humans.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.430
And then check this out.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.780
When its missions are complete,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.490
The x-37B deorbits and lands
back on Earth like an airplane.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.740
- That's why the x-37 is
an amazing capability.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.340
It's reusable, it's
returnable, it's refurbishable,

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.200
but it isn't an enormous
vehicle that's limited

00:01:06.064 --> 00:01:07.020
by having to have humans on board.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.470
- Because it's uncrewed,
the x-37B can stay in space

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.290
for years and Boeing, the
company that makes it,

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.590
says that since 2010, it
has completed six missions,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.780
traveled 1.3 billion miles

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.780
and deployed for more
than 900 days straight.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.380
So, what does the x-37B
do when it's in space?

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.780
The official answer is lots and lots

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:29.700
of classified experiments.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.080
Take a look at this animation.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.560
You can see the x-37B
flying with its doors open,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.140
which enables it to
expose materials in space

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.570
and carry out all kinds
of different tests.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.100
We do have a little bit of insight

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.470
into some of the experiments
it's done in the past.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.560
For example, we know
that the x-37B has hosted

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.030
a power beaming system,

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.490
technology that could
one day enable satellites

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.560
to send solar power down to Earth.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.440
And we also know it carried
an Air Force Academy satellite

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.300
into space before deploying it.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.370
The experts I talked to
said it could also be used

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.350
to test materials for satellites

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.930
or space sensors in
various parts of space.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.510
- This is national security related,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.180
to counter the Russian,
Chinese capabilities

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.230
that are coming up.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.090
- There are many, many experiments

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.740
and many things you
would wanna do in space

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.260
that frankly we would
not want peer competitors

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.830
to know about just as
they hide things from us.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.110
- So let's talk about
some of the speculation,

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.920
like that the x-37B is
some kind of space bomber

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.930
or that it could be used to test weapons.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.580
- There isn't a lot of common sense

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.730
behind trying to do
offensive weapons in space.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.530
They sound great in science fiction,

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.880
but for many practical reasons

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.140
they don't make a lot of sense.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.730
But no, there's absolutely no evidence

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.640
that x-37 has been doing
anything offensive in space.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.760
- This painting unveiled by
the US Space Operations Command

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.760
also helped fuel
speculation that the x-37B

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.300
could be used to intercept
adversary satellites.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.340
That's because amateur
space watchers said,

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.400
Hey, that futuristic space
vehicle they're depicting,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.560
that looks a lot like the x-37B.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.393
- It's plausible.

00:02:59.393 --> 00:03:01.980
You can take out satellites by going close

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.710
and blinding it with lasers
or something like that.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.630
It's all sorts of possibilities,

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.270
- But interfering with a
satellite is a little different

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.790
than actually scooping one out of the sky.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.280
- So, it actually turns
out to be really difficult

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.760
to do an intercept of an
object in space from space

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.280
for the very simple reason
that when you are in orbit

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.930
around the Earth, you're traveling

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.060
at a very, very high
speed, a high velocity.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.800
- After launching on its seventh mission,

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.710
the x-37B could be
heading deeper into space

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:29.850
than ever before.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.610
And that's why this recent
launch is getting a lot of buzz.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:35.010
Not only did it blast
off on a falcon heavy,

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.670
which Space X says is capable
of going as far as Mars,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.520
but the Space Force dropped a
few hints in press releases,

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.530
saying that the vehicle will be operating

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.450
in new orbital regimes,

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.750
experimenting with space
domain awareness technologies,

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:52.260
and investigating radiation
effects to NASA materials.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.810
That means the spacecraft
is probably going

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.870
beyond low Earth orbit where
it has operated before,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.290
and it could potentially
even travel 22,000 miles out

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.030
to geosynchronous orbit.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.370
- There are a lot of
really interesting orbits

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.110
that give you new capabilities

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.180
that cover different parts of the planet.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.890
As an example, the Russians
have for many, many years

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.620
used a type of orbit
called a Molniya orbit,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:19.110
which is a very high-inclination orbit.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.240
So it takes 'em up to very high altitude

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.980
and then drops down to low altitude,

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.990
and they can use those orbits

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.050
to get more time over a
certain part of the Earth.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.400
It gives you other advantages

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.540
that the Russians have utilized.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.150
- The radiation clue in
Space Force's press release

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.780
could also suggest that the
x-37B will be spending time

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.050
exposing materials in the
Van Allen radiation belts,

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.230
which have been deemed deadly
to some types of materials.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.550
- You have to take that into account

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.030
if you're going to establish
a satellite constellation

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:48.863
higher up.

00:04:48.863 --> 00:04:50.914
- But of course, these professors say

00:04:50.914 --> 00:04:53.370
these are just educated guesses,
since no one really knows

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.440
where the x-37B is heading.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.210
Against the backdrop of all of this

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.270
is an intensifying space
race between superpowers,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.980
and that includes growing competition

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.010
to develop and build more space planes.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:08.040
The NASA-contracted
Sierra Space Dream Chaser

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.230
could potentially fly this year,

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.180
and while Russia hasn't made much progress

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.390
on its space planes in
recent decades, China has.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:19.260
- We know that China has been
eagerly pursuing space planes

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.760
for quite some time.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.000
- The US says Beijing has been
developing two space planes,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.130
though details have been kept very secret

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.890
and they've been years
behind the US in flying them.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.830
After one of them launched in
December, General Saltzman,

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.740
the chief of Space Operations
for the US Space Force

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.200
said that that plane and the x-37B

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.560
are some of the most-watched
objects in orbit right now.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.780
And he said it is no
coincidence that China

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.741
is trying to match the US's
timing and capabilities.

00:05:46.741 --> 00:05:49.241
(tense music)

